["07:00"]={"She locked herself in, made no reply to my bonjour through the door; she was up at \003seven o’clock\004, the samovar was taken in to her from the kitchen.","Crime and Punishment","Fyodor Dostoyevsky"},
["07:01"]={"I took the first tentative step towards finding out at \003one minute past seven\004 the next morning, in Fort Bird’s mortuary.","The Enemy","Lee Child"},
["07:02"]={"\00307:02\004:18 One and a half hours. “Case,” she said, “I wanna favour.”","Neuromancer","William Gibson"},
["07:03"]={"\0037:03 a.m.\004 Return to bed in sulk over weight. Head-state bad. Sleeping or getting up equally out of question. Think about Daniel.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["07:04"]={"\0037:04 A.M.\004\nStone felt his consciousness returning as the blast of an engine cut through his sedative‑induced reverie. Where was he? There were vibrations all around him and a deafening roar that was slowly spiraling upward in frequency and volume.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:05"]={"Outside my window the sky hung low and gray. It looked like snow, which added to my malaise. The clock read \003five after seven\004. I punched the remote control and watched the morning news as I lay in bed.","Dance Dance Dance","Haruki Murakami"},
["07:07"]={"When Joubert walked into the parade room at \003seven minutes past seven\004 on the first of January, forty detectives were already seated on the blue-gray government-issue chairs placed in a large rectangle against the four walls.","Dead Before Dying","Deon Meyer"},
["07:08"]={"Reacher had no watch but he figured when he saw Gregory it must have been \003between eight and nine minutes after seven o’clock\004.","The Hard Way","Lee Child"},
["07:09"]={"The morning house lay empty. The clock ticked on, repeating and repeating its sounds into the emptiness. \003Seven-nine\004, breakfast time, seven-nine!","There Will Come Soft Rains","Ray Bradbury"},
["07:10"]={"A search in Bradshaw informed me that a train left St. Pancras at \0037:10\004, which would land me at any Galloway station in the late afternoon.","The Thirty-Nine Steps","John Buchan"},
["07:11"]={"Anyway, every morning at \003eleven minutes past seven\004 he’d slam the door and rev the engine like he was starting a grand prix, ruining my beauty sleep, especially if I’d just come off nights.","Limestone Cowboy","Stuart Pawson"},
["07:12"]={"At \003twelve minutes past seven\004, in the kitchen, Kimberly was becoming anxious. She had been told by Sister Holland that Miss Gradwyn had asked for her early-morning tea tray to be brought up at seven o’clock.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["07:14"]={"I jump onto Rocker to look at Watch, he says \00307:14\004. I can skateboard on Rocker without holding on to her, then I whee back onto Duvet and I’m snowboarding instead.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["07:15"]={"At \0037:15 A.M.\004, January 25th, we started flying northwestward under McTighe’s pilotage with ten men, seven dogs, a sledge, a fuel and food supply, and other items including the plane’s wireless outfit.","At the Mountains of Madness","H.P. Lovecraft"},
["07:17"]={"As of \0037:17 am\004 local time on 30 June 1908, Padzhitnoff had been working for nearly a year as a contract employee of the Okhrana, receiving five hundred rubles a month, a sum which hovered at the exorbitant end of spy-budget outlays for those years.","Against the Day","Thomas Pynchon"},
["07:18"]={"\0037:18 A.M.\004\n“Ulysses to Sirene. Do you read me?”\nWhen his radio crackled, Armont was in the medical facility of the Bates Motel, watching as a plasma IV was attached to Dimitri’s arm. He immediately grabbed for it.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:19"]={"I opened the sunroof and turned up the CD player volume to combat fatigue, and at \0037:19 am\004 on Saturday, with the caffeine still running all around my brain, Jackson Browne and I pulled into Moree.","The Rosie Project","Graeme Simsion"},
["07:20"]={"At \0037:20\004, the door swung open and Anne reappeared to carry out her most important function of the day. “Time to take you through to the studio, Harry.”","Cometh the Hour","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:21"]={"Why it felt important to know the time she didn’t know, other than to try and root herself in the midst of this chaos. \0037:21 a.m.\004 So many people would have been eating breakfast, getting ready for work or the Passover holiday.","The Little Wartime Library","Kate Thompson"},
["07:23"]={"Sebastian had to borrow his mother’s alarm clock to make sure he was up in time to catch the \0037:23\004 to Paddington. Emma was waiting for him in the hall and offered to drive him to Temple Meads. It soon became clear why.","Best Kept Secret","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:24"]={"There was a brief murmur of voices; then Stephen Courtney-Brigs followed her into the sitting-room. Glancing at the clock, Dalgliesh saw that the hands stood at \0037:24 a.m.\004 The working day had almost begun.","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["07:25"]={"At \003twenty-five minutes past seven\004: Ker Karraje, Engineer Serko and Captain Spade advance to the extermity of the point, where they sweep the north-western horizon with their telescopes.","Facing the Flag","Jules Verne"},
["07:26"]={"Chuck was on deck at \003twenty-six minutes past seven\004 when marines in helmets and backpacks began to swarm down the rope nets hanging over the sides of the ship and jump into the high-sided landing craft.","Winter of the World","Ken Follett"},
["07:27"]={"The pilot welcomed them aboard and warned them there might be a slight delay. Dexter checked his watch: \0037:27\004. He began drumming his fingers on the armrest that divided him from Scott.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:28"]={"As you know, we’re on twenty-four hour call and I got here at \003seven twenty-eight\004. We decided to start the investigation at once. The undertakers will collect the body as soon as you’ve finished.","The Murder Room","P.D. James"},
["07:29"]={"At \0037:29\004 in the morning of 1 July, the cinematographer finds himself filming silence itself.","At Break of Day","Elizabeth Speller"},
["07:30"]={"Precisely at \003half past seven\004 the station-master came into the traffic office. He weighed almost sixteen stone, but women always said that he was incredibly light on his feet when he danced.","Closely Observed Trains","Bohumil Hrabal"},
["07:31"]={"\0037:31 A.M.\004\nBill Bates looked through the Sikorsky’s wide windscreen and saw them coming. The time had arrived, he realized immediately, to make a move. Now or never.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:32"]={"At \0037:32\004, he suffered a fatal stroke.","It","Stephen King"},
["07:33"]={"Wednesday \0037:33 A.M.\004\n“You’re lucky I love this spot,” Vance said, gazing out over the city. “Nothing else on the planet could have got me up this early in the morning.”","Project Daedalus","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:34"]={"\0037:34\004. Monday morning, Blackeberg. The burglar alarm at the ICA grocery store on Arvid Morne’s way is set off.","Let the Right One In","John Ajvide Lindqvist"},
["07:35"]={"Florentyna Kane did not wake until \0037:35\004. She rolled over, trying to recall the dream she had just had, but none of it would come back to her, so she let her mind wander.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:36"]={"\0037:36\004, sunrise. The hospital blinds were much better, darker than her own.","Let the Right One In","John Ajvide Lindqvist"},
["07:37"]={"My telephone rang at \003twenty-three minutes to eight\004, just as I put a cup of coffee down on the breakfast table.","Satellite People","Has Olav Lahlum"},
["07:38"]={"\0037:38 A.M.\004\n“I copy,” Nichols said into his mike. “When did the chopper lift off?”","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:39"]={"At \0037:39\004 the aircraft taxied onto the runway to prepare for takeoff. When it stopped, Dexter asked the flight attendant what was holding them up.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:40"]={"\0037:40 a.m.\004 Have breakfast.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["07:41"]={"He rushed downstairs. The hall was empty; \003nineteen minutes to eight\004! The train left at eight o’clock. Had he time to saddle Bolero?","The Dark Flower","John Galsworthy"},
["07:42"]={"So he really had no choice but to pay an occasional visit to the living room instead, where the hands on the grandfather clock now indicated, rather unambiguously, that it was \0037:42\004.","The Lincoln Highway","Amor Towles"},
["07:43"]={"It was \003seventeen minutes to eight\004. It seemed to me that should give me plenty of leeway, but I hadn’t been there five minutes before I started to worry that I’d missed him.","The Burglar Who Thought He Was Bogart","Lawrence Block"},
["07:44"]={"She voices her thoughts: “It’s not exactly how you’d choose to go, is it? You’d rather die flying a kite with your grandchildren, or at a great party or something. Not on the \003seven forty-four\004.”","One Moment, One Morning","Sarah Rayner"},
["07:45"]={"I was doing my exercises and wondering where he could have got to, because it was already \003seven forty-five\004 and he still had not come out.","Wild detectives","Roberto Bolaño"},
["07:46"]={"He awoke with a start. The clock on his bedside table said \0037:46 a.m.\004 He cursed, jumped out of bed and dressed. He stuffed his toothbrush and toothpaste in his jacket pocket, and parked outside the station just before 8 a.m. In reception, Ebba beckoned to him.","The Dogs of Riga","Henning Mankell"},
["07:47"]={"He looked across at his son. ‘You been booking in all those names, the way I taught you?’\n‘Sure have, Dad. Mr Parnell, \0037:47\004; Mr Parker, 8:09; Mr Tudor-Jones, 8:11; Mr Alexander, 8:23.’","The Grass is Always Greener","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:48"]={"\0037:48 A.M.\004\nVance stared up the mountain, puzzled. The silence baffled him, and then he realized why. He was not hearing the usual high-tension hum of transformers; nothing was operating. They had shut down the power.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["07:49"]={"\003Eleven minutes to eight\004.\n“You’re always right; there must be a clock in your head.”","The End of the Beginning","Ray Bradbury"},
["07:50"]={"DI Hogan rang the front doorbell at \003ten minutes to eight\004. It was opened a few moments later by someone who was clean-shaven, smartly dressed and clearly expecting him.","Next in Line","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:51"]={"The plane swung around onto the take-off runway at \0037:51\004, its jets revving before it moved slowly forward, then gathered speed. The wheels left the ground at 7:53.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:52"]={"Homicide Detective David Neiser arrived at the house on Twin Peaks Drive at \003eight minutes to eight\004. Chief Criminal Deputy Joe Doench was already there.","In the Still of the Night","Ann Rule"},
["07:53"]={"The plane swung around onto the take-off runway at 7:51, its jets revving before it moved slowly forward, then gathered speed. The wheels left the ground at \0037:53\004.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:54"]={"When I awoke on the arrival of the others, it was \003six minutes to eight in the morning\004 of the same day, today. Not two hours had passed from my rising, and time was back to normal. But the things that happened in that time could never be compressed into two hours.","The Six Fingers of Time","R.A. Lafferty"},
["07:55"]={"Maybe now isn’t the best time for you to see her, Mr. Dresden.\nI glanced up at the clock on the wall. It was \003five minutes before eight\004. “She wanted me early.” I stepped to one side to go around him.","Fool Moon","Jim Butcher"},
["07:56"]={"The Castle Gate — only the Castle Gate — and it was \003four minutes to eight\004.","Buddenbrooks","Thomas Mann"},
["07:57"]={"Emma read the detailed submissions from both presidents during her journey across London, but hadn’t come down in favor of either side by the time her car pulled into Harley Street. She placed the file back in the red box and checked her watch: \0037:57\004.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["07:58"]={"McEnany looked at the clock in the corner of the video screen. It said \0037:58 AM\004. A few more keystrokes, and Paige Caldwell’s voice came through his headset.","Murderer’s Row","Ray Keating"},
["07:59"]={"One morning, I had just arrived at the house and it was \003not yet eight\004 when I found Don Octavio up, waiting for me in the kitchen.","Wild detectives","Roberto Bolaño"},
